you know chris got hit  you know in the knees yesterday which is  a play that i think they ought to  take out of the game of football uh from  a receiver standpoint you know i've kind  of  talked to the pa about it for a while  about  you know and i'd like to speak to the  rules competition committee at some  point this offseason to i've seen that  hit too many times where a defenseless  pass catcher is in the process of  catching a ball then he's hit by the  defender and you know a lot of the  defenders will say well we can't hit him  in the head anymore  well the point is you can't hit anyone  in the head anymore and you can't hit  any one of these anymore except for  receivers because you can still hit them  in the knees which doesn't make any  sense to me  um you can't hit a defensive lineman in  the knees  you can't hit a punter in the knees you  can't hit a quarterback at the knees you  can't hit a db in the knees  except we're somehow allowing  hits on defenseless receivers in these  so  now it needs to be addressed and it  needs to be really thought out it really  impacts guys careers and and chris you  know i know he'll overcome it  so it's a tough rehab but you know you  you tear your acl that's that's a  lifelong injury  you know and i'm sure almost every pass  catcher in the nfl would prefer  hit to the head over a hit to the knees  i certainly would i take that you know  million out of a million  it's it's it's amazing man tom said  basically everything that i said the  other day and  my whole thing was protect your brother  you know what i'm saying protect your  brother you got to understand i like pj  with excuse me i like pj williams when i  called him out it wasn't because the hit  was dirty necessarily dirty okay it was  a clean hit by nfl standards but to me  it was a dirty hit because pj williams  he's a very smart guy he's played all  the positions in the secondary he's a  very versatile guy so he's a very smart  guy when he hit godwin on the knees he  immediately got up and celebrated he  didn't so he intentionally he wanted to  hit him at his knees and all i'm saying  is look man we're all trying to make a  living why would you hit him up there  you asked any player in any sport female  male in any sport would you rather get  hit in the knee or would you rather get  hit in the shoulder they're gonna 100  out of 100 times they're going to say  hit me up in the upper body because now  i have a chance to get up and walk away  i get a chance to get up and literally  walk away but when you go at somebody's  knees and tom is 100 spot on you don't  go at their knees because we are  brothers i can't take away your  opportunity to make millions and  millions of dollars check this out chris  godwin signed a one-year 15 million  dollar deal one year 15 million dollar  deal he could have he could have gone  many other places got 50 60 million  dollars or 40 million dollars guaranteed  and and secured the bag he sacrificed  for that situation and now all of a  sudden what team is going to go and pay  chris godwin four years 60 million and  guarantee 40 million because he's coming  off an ac injury so what he's got to do  he's got to sign another one-year deal  go through an entire season  17 weeks 18 weeks plus playoffs and see  if he can stay healthy to go get his  money so that's why i tell players all  the time these teams have money they're  very very wealthy you got to secure the  bag always get your money don't  sacrifice for anybody  well i completely agree so let me start  there and and something that stood out  from what tom said was that receiver is  the only position that we let hits like  this occur through that resonated with  me right you can't do it to a  quarterback that's completely out of the  game you can't do it to a defensive line  that's complete out of game can't do it  to an offensive line that's completely  out of the game so you can't do it to  anybody else now how the hell are you  going to look at me and say that a  receiver can't do it to a kicker after a  kick how the hell are you going to look  at me and say that a receiver who's  catching the ball with his head turned  running full speed and getting hit from  a place that he doesn't even know is  coming that that could be a legal hit it  just makes no sense and to hear tom go a  million out of a million i would take  the high hit over the low hit well why  aren't we talking to the players then  before we're making this rule and this  has been one that hasn't made sense to  me for a long time we've seen gronk take  these shots i thought gronk after the  first hit we both thought this rod that  he was looking a little tentative out  there after that massive shot  let's be clear i mean this was a game  where new orleans came in and from the  opening whistle was the more physical  team they were physically just pushing  around tampa in their own stadium in  every single way but i will say that i  thought that pj williams shot low it  changed gronk it changed some of those  weapons i just thought it looked like  tampa was playing tentative from then on  out  absolutely it was spot on i mean you  look at gronk gronk like gronk when  you've had injuries to your knee  you think about that you say oh my god i  don't want to go across the middle no  send me out to the you know to the  sideline i don't want to come across the  middle it changed the very nature of the  game because you saw even um tyler  johnson he was in the game he went  across the middle he's peeking and  looking and i'm like it just me you and  i we talked about it completely changed  the you know the nature of the game  i do think that they will go back and  look at that as we take a look at some  of gronk's plays and he just always  looks sort of half speed and anytime  they would take a close shot of his face  he just looked nervous dropping balls  he's looking he's looking up for the hit  before he's even making the catch and he  had the biggest drop of the night on  that deep one late in the game where he  just never even saw it he was what brady  put the perfect throw down the sideline  and he just didn't look up to see it  right there there it was  yeah fournette told me that rob  gronkowski is the guy that brings all  the energy to this team and he didn't  have any energy we're looking at like  rob is normally a lot more you know  active and excited he just kind of out  there he looked tired he looked like he  was out of shape i'm like what's going  on with rob gronkowski but that hit  really set the tone  and it wasn't the only hit right i mean  i i can remember a handful of other big  hits even the one where fournette got  spun around i mean he they spun him in a  full 360. and fournette leaves the game  i mean it they came in there and they  just pushed him around  hi i'm mike tarico and thanks for  watching make sure to hit subscribe for  the latest news and highlights from nbc  sports

